# Analyzer-eval local config — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy this file to `eval.properties` (same directory) and set your local path.
# `eval.properties` is git-ignored, so your machine-specific path is never committed.
#
# Resolution order for every key (first non-blank wins):
#   1. -D system property  (e.g. -Ddisc.eval.projectPath=...)
#   2. environment variable (only DISC_EVAL_PROJECT_PATH, for the path)
#   3. this file
#
# When disc.eval.projectPath is unset/blank or not a directory, AnalyzerEvalTest
# SKIPS (it never fails) — so a normal `./gradlew test` stays green.

# REQUIRED — absolute path to a Java project to scan for codebase grounding.
# Use a project that does NOT already contain a discount-rule type (a clean
# spring-petclinic checkout is ideal).
disc.eval.projectPath=/absolute/path/to/spring-petclinic

# OPTIONAL — model to run the analyzer with. Must be one of Models.ALLOWED:
#   claude-sonnet-4-6 | claude-opus-4-8 | claude-opus-4-7 | claude-haiku-4-5
# Omit (or leave blank) to use the claude CLI default.
#disc.eval.model=claude-opus-4-8

# OPTIONAL — how many times each fixture runs (stability). Default 1.
# The Gate stability standard is 5 consecutive green runs per fixture:
#   ./gradlew test --tests '*AnalyzerEvalTest' -Ddisc.eval.runs=5
#disc.eval.runs=5
